{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Remove your sandals.</b> Cast off your sandals, from the root of ״כי ישל זיתך״, ״ונשל גויים רבים״." "<b>From upon your feet.</b> Because sometimes one steps in a place of filth. And since even that which is for the hand is called נעל without qualification, as it is written ״שלף איש נעלו״, whose Aramaic translation is 'he drew the scabbard of his right hand,' it was necessary to say here ״מעל רגלך״. And so our Rabbis said (Berakhot 54a): a person may not enter the Temple Mount with his sandal on his foot, for this is reverence for the Temple." "<b>For the place where you stand</b> etc. Every place where you find the Shekhinah preceding to speak to His prophet — as here, where it preceded in the bush, and with Joshua, and at the giving of the Torah — there you find the place holy. But in other places where He revealed Himself, as we find with many prophets, the place is not holy."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:57.770520354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}